  "rocm_rocsolver_finding": {
    "issue": "When PirateNet initializes block skip gates at alpha=0 (nonlinearity=0.0), step-1 PirateBlock dense gradients are zero (GG=0), causing float32 rocsolver_ssyevd (eigh) on AMD MI300X (ROCm 6.2) to raise LinAlgError on repeated zero eigenvalues. At steps 3-5, block preconditioner entries (~4.65e-21) lie below sqrt(FLT_MIN) (1.084e-19), causing float32 rocsolver_sgeqrf (qr) to underflow on squared column norms and return non-orthogonal matrices (||Q^T Q - I||_inf > 4e4).",
    "fix": "Normalize power_iter by its maximum magnitude before QR, promote ROCm (and qr_dtype='float64') eigensolver/QR factorizations to float64, verify ||Q^T Q - I||_inf <= 1e-2, and fall back to CPU LAPACK float64 on failure (verified ||Q^T Q - I||_inf <= 8.35e-7 on MI300X)."
  },
